{"id":"mahabharata-8-059","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":59,"title":"एकोनषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 59 · Arjuna against the Kaurava army","summary":{"en":"The Kaurava champions rush at Arjuna with his monkey banner, and elephants and horses fall and flee. The Panchala heroes attack Karna's army while many chariot-warriors go down.","kn":"ಕಪಿಧ್ವಜದ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಮೇಲೆ ಕೌರವ ವೀರರು ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಆನೆ, ಕುದುರೆಗಳು ಬಿದ್ದು ಓಡುತ್ತವೆ. ಪಾಂಚಾಲ ವೀರರು ಕರ್ಣನ ಸೈನ್ಯದ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅನೇಕ ರಥಿಕರು ಉರುಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"कपिध्वज अर्जुन पर कौरव वीर टूटते हैं, और हाथी-घोड़े गिरते और भागते हैं। पाञ्चाल वीर कर्ण की सेना पर आक्रमण करते हैं और अनेक रथी गिरते हैं।","te":"కపిధ్వజుడైన అర్జునునిపై కౌరవ వీరులు దూకుతారు; ఏనుగులు, గుర్రాలు కూలి పారిపోతాయి. పాంచాల వీరులు కర్ణుని సేనపై దాడి చేస్తారు; అనేక రథికులు కూలతారు.","ta":"குரங்குக்கொடி அர்ஜுனன் மீது கௌரவ வீரர் பாய, யானை குதிரைகள் வீழ்ந்து ஓடுகின்றன. பாஞ்சால வீரர் கர்ணனின் படையைத் தாக்க, பல தேர்வீரர் சாய்கின்றனர்.","ml":"കുരങ്ങിന്റെ കൊടിയുള്ള അർജുനനെതിരെ കൗരവ വീരന്മാർ കുതിച്ചെത്തുന്നു; ആനകളും കുതിരകളും വീണ് ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു. പാഞ്ചാല വീരന്മാർ കർണ്ണന്റെ സേനയെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; രഥയോദ്ധാക്കളിൽ പലരും വീഴുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.59; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तं तु यान्तं महावेगैरश्वैः कपिवरध्वजम् ।\nयुद्धायाभ्यद्रवन्वीराः कुरूणां नवती रथाः ।\nपरिवव्रुर्नरव्याघ्रा नरव्याघ्रं रणेऽर्जुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Arjuna, whose banner bore the great ape, drove on with his swift horses, ninety Kuru chariot-warriors, tigers among men, ran at him to fight and surrounded that tiger among men in the battle."}},{"n":2,"text":"कृष्णः श्वेतान्महावेगानश्वान्कनकभूषणान् ।\nमुक्ताजालप्रतिच्छन्नान्प्रैषीत्कर्णरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna drove his swift white horses, adorned with gold and covered in nets of pearls, toward Karna's chariot."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः कर्णरथं यान्तमरीन्घ्नन्तं धनंजयम् ।\nबाणवर्षैरभिघ्नन्तः संशप्तकरथा ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Dhananjaya went toward Karna's chariot, killing his enemies, the chariots of the Samshaptakas struck at him with showers of arrows."}},{"n":4,"text":"त्वरमाणांस्तु तान्सर्वान्ससूतेष्वसनध्वजान् ।\nजघान नवतिं वीरानर्जुनो निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna killed all those ninety hasty heroes, with their drivers, bows and banners, using sharp arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"तेऽपतन्त हता बाणैर्नानारूपैः किरीटिना ।\nसविमाना यथा सिद्धाः स्वर्गात्पुण्यक्षये तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by the diadem-wearer's arrows of many kinds, they fell like Siddhas dropping from heaven in their celestial cars when their merit is spent."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततः सरथनागाश्वाः कुरवः कुरुसत्तम ।\nनिर्भया भरतश्रेष्ठमभ्यवर्तन्त फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O best of the Kurus, the Kurus with their chariots, elephants and horses fearlessly came against Phalguna, the best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":7,"text":"तदायस्तममुक्तास्त्रमुदीर्णवरवारणम् ।\nपुत्राणां ते महत्सैन्यं समरौत्सीद्धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya held back that great army of your sons, though its weapons were raised and its splendid elephants had charged."}},{"n":8,"text":"शक्त्यृष्टितोमरप्रासैर्गदानिस्त्रिंशसायकैः ।\nप्राच्छादयन्महेष्वासाः कुरवः कुरुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archers of the Kurus covered the Kuru delight, Arjuna, with spears, lances, javelins, darts, maces, swords and arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"तां कुरूणां प्रविततां शस्त्रवृष्टिं समुद्यताम् ।\nव्यधमत्पाण्डवो बाणैस्तमः सूर्य इवांशुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava scattered that spreading, uplifted storm of Kuru weapons with his arrows, as the sun drives off darkness with its rays."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो म्लेच्छाः स्थितैर्मत्तैस्त्रयोदशशतैर्गजैः ।\nपार्श्वतोऽभ्यहनन्पार्थं तव पुत्रस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, at the command of your son, barbarian Mlechchhas with thirteen hundred standing, rutting elephants attacked Partha from the flank."}},{"n":11,"text":"कर्णिनालीकनाराचैस्तोमरैः प्रासशक्तिभिः ।\nकम्पनैर्भिण्डिपालैश्च रथस्थं पार्थमार्दयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With barbed arrows, long darts, iron shafts, javelins, lances, spears, iron clubs and slings they pressed upon Partha in his chariot."}},{"n":12,"text":"तामस्त्रवृष्टिं प्रहितां द्विपस्थैर्यवनैः स्मयन् ।\nचिच्छेद निशितैर्भल्लैरर्धचन्द्रैश्च फल्गुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Smiling, Phalguna cut down that rain of missiles hurled by the Yavanas riding the elephants, using sharp broad-headed and crescent arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"अथ तान्द्विरदान्सर्वान्नानालिङ्गैर्महाशरैः ।\nसपताकान्सहारोहान्गिरीन्वज्रैरिवाभिनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with great arrows marked in many ways, he split all those elephants, with their banners and riders, as thunderbolts split mountains."}},{"n":14,"text":"ते हेमपुङ्खैरिषुभिराचिता हेममालिनः ।\nहताः पेतुर्महानागाः साग्निज्वाला इवाद्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Studded with gold-feathered arrows and wearing garlands of gold, the great elephants fell dead, like mountains blazing with fire."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो गाण्डीवनिर्घोषो महानासीद्विशां पते ।\nस्तनतां कूजतां चैव मनुष्यगजवाजिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of people, there was a great din of the Gandiva, mixed with the roars and cries of men, elephants and horses."}},{"n":16,"text":"कुञ्जराश्च हता राजन्प्राद्रवंस्ते समन्ततः ।\nअश्वाश्च पर्यधावन्त हतारोहा दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"The elephants, struck down, fled on every side, O king, and the horses whose riders were slain ran off in all ten directions."}},{"n":17,"text":"रथा हीना महाराज रथिभिर्वाजिभिस्तथा ।\nगन्धर्वनगराकारा दृश्यन्ते स्म सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, chariots bereft of their warriors and horses were seen by the thousand, looking like cities of the Gandharvas."}},{"n":18,"text":"अश्वारोहा महाराज धावमानास्ततस्ततः ।\nतत्र तत्रैव दृश्यन्ते पतिताः पार्थसायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, horsemen running here and there were seen fallen in one spot after another, brought down by Partha's arrows."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मिन्क्षणे पाण्डवस्य बाह्वोर्बलमदृश्यत ।\nयत्सादिनो वारणांश्च रथांश्चैकोऽजयद्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that moment the strength of the Pandava's arms was plain to see, for alone he overcame in battle the horsemen, elephants and chariots."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्त्र्यङ्गेण महता बलेन भरतर्षभ ।\nदृष्ट्वा परिवृतं राजन्भीमसेनः किरीटिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"O best of the Bharatas, Bhimasena then saw the diadem-wearer surrounded by a great army of three arms."}},{"n":21,"text":"हतावशेषानुत्सृज्य त्वदीयान्कतिचिद्रथान् ।\nजवेनाभ्यद्रवद्राजन्धनंजयरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving aside a few of your chariots that were all that remained of the slain, he rushed swiftly to Dhananjaya's chariot, O king."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततस्तत्प्राद्रवत्सैन्यं हतभूयिष्ठमातुरम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा यदर्जुनं भीमो जगाम भ्रातरं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that army, mostly slaughtered and distressed, fled when it saw that Bhima had gone toward Arjuna, his brother."}},{"n":23,"text":"हतावशिष्टांस्तुरगानर्जुनेन महाजवान् ।\nभीमो व्यधमदभ्रान्तो गदापाणिर्महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unflinching, with a mace in hand, Bhima in that great battle destroyed the swift horses that Arjuna had left alive."}},{"n":24,"text":"कालरात्रिमिवात्युग्रां नरनागाश्वभोजनाम् ।\nप्राकाराट्टपुरद्वारदारणीमतिदारुणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His mace was like a most savage night of Time, feeding on men, elephants and horses, and terrible in breaking ramparts, towers and city gates."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततो गदां नृनागाश्वेष्वाशु भीमो व्यवासृजत् ।\nसा जघान बहूनश्वानश्वारोहांश्च मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima swiftly hurled the mace among the men, elephants and horses, and it struck down many horses and horsemen, my lord."}},{"n":26,"text":"कांस्यायसतनुत्रांस्तान्नरानश्वांश्च पाण्डवः ।\nपोथयामास गदया सशब्दं तेऽपतन्हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava crushed with his mace those men and horses in armor of bronze and iron, and they fell dead with a crash."}},{"n":27,"text":"हत्वा तु तद्गजानीकं भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nपुनः स्वरथमास्थाय पृष्ठतोऽर्जुनमन्वगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having destroyed that elephant force, mighty Bhimasena mounted his own chariot again and followed behind Arjuna."}},{"n":28,"text":"हतं पराङ्मुखप्रायं निरुत्साहं परं बलम् ।\nव्यालम्बत महाराज प्रायशः शस्त्रवेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The enemy force, slain, mostly turned back and dispirited, hung back, O great king, in a state almost entangled in its weapons."}},{"n":29,"text":"विलम्बमानं तत्सैन्यमप्रगल्भमवस्थितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा प्राच्छादयद्बाणैरर्जुनः प्राणतापनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that army lingering, timid and standing still, Arjuna covered it with arrows that scorched the life out of men."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततः कुरूणामभवदार्तनादो महामृधे ।\nरथाश्वनागासुहरैर्वध्यतामर्जुनेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kurus raised a cry of anguish in that great battle, as Arjuna's arrows, which took the lives of chariots, horses and elephants, slew them."}},{"n":31,"text":"हाहाकृतं भृशं तस्थौ लीयमानं परस्परम् ।\nअलातचक्रवत्सैन्यं तदाभ्रमत तावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crying out in dismay, they stood pressed against one another, and your army whirled like a wheel of fire."}},{"n":32,"text":"आदीप्तं तव तत्सैन्यं शरैश्छिन्नतनुच्छदम् ।\nआसीत्स्वशोणितक्लिन्नं फुल्लाशोकवनं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your blazing army, its armor cut away by arrows and soaked in its own blood, looked like a grove of aśoka trees in full bloom."}},{"n":33,"text":"तद्दृष्ट्वा कुरवस्तत्र विक्रान्तं सव्यसाचिनः ।\nनिराशाः समपद्यन्त सर्वे कर्णस्य जीविते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the prowess of Savyasachin there, all the Kurus fell into despair about Karna's survival."}},{"n":34,"text":"अविषह्यं तु पार्थस्य शरसंपातमाहवे ।\nमत्वा न्यवर्तन्कुरवो जिता गाण्डीवधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking Partha's rain of arrows in battle unbearable, the Kurus, defeated by the wielder of the Gandiva, turned back."}},{"n":35,"text":"ते हित्वा समरे पार्थं वध्यमानाश्च सायकैः ।\nप्रदुद्रुवुर्दिशो भीताश्चुक्रुशुश्चापि सूतजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abandoning Partha in the battle and struck by arrows, they fled in fear in every direction, calling out to Karna the charioteer's son."}},{"n":36,"text":"अभ्यद्रवत तान्पार्थः किरञ्शरशतान्बहून् ।\nहर्षयन्पाण्डवान्योधान्भीमसेनपुरोगमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha pursued them, scattering many hundreds of arrows and cheering the Pandava warriors led by Bhimasena."}},{"n":37,"text":"पुत्रास्तु ते महाराज जग्मुः कर्णरथं प्रति ।\nअगाधे मज्जतां तेषां द्वीपः कर्णोऽभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"But your sons, great king, went to Karna's chariot, and for them, sinking in deep water, Karna then became an island."}},{"n":38,"text":"कुरवो हि महाराज निर्विषाः पन्नगा इव ।\nकर्णमेवोपलीयन्त भयाद्गाण्डीवधन्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus, O great king, clung to Karna alone out of fear of the wielder of the Gandiva, like snakes whose venom is gone."}},{"n":39,"text":"यथा सर्वाणि भूतानि मृत्योर्भीतानि भारत ।\nधर्ममेवोपलीयन्ते कर्मवन्ति हि यानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Bharata, as all creatures frightened of death take refuge in dharma alone, or those who have deeds to their credit do so,"}},{"n":40,"text":"तथा कर्णं महेष्वासं पुत्रास्तव नराधिप ।\nउपालीयन्त संत्रासात्पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"so, O lord of men, your sons in terror sought refuge in Karna, the great archer, from the great-souled Pandava."}},{"n":41,"text":"ताञ्शोणितपरिक्लिन्नान्विषमस्थाञ्शरातुरान् ।\nमा भैष्टेत्यब्रवीत्कर्णो ह्यभितो मामितेति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna told those bloodied, battered, arrow-tormented men in difficulty, \"Do not be afraid; come to me from every side.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"संभग्नं हि बलं दृष्ट्वा बलात्पार्थेन तावकम् ।\nधनुर्विस्फारयन्कर्णस्तस्थौ शत्रुजिघांसया ।\nपाञ्चालान्पुनराधावत्पश्यतः सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your army broken by Partha's force, Karna stood stretching his bow, eager to kill his enemies, and ran again against the Panchalas, as Savyasachin looked on."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततः क्षणेन क्षितिपाः क्षतजप्रतिमेक्षणाः ।\nकर्णं ववर्षुर्बाणौघैर्यथा मेघा महीधरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in an instant kings with eyes red as blood showered Karna with floods of arrows, as clouds do a mountain."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततः शरसहस्राणि कर्णमुक्तानि मारिष ।\nव्ययोजयन्त पाञ्चालान्प्राणैः प्राणभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, my lord, the thousands of arrows loosed by Karna, best of those who live, parted the Panchalas from their lives."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततो रणो महानासीत्पाञ्चालानां विशां पते ।\nवध्यतां सूतपुत्रेण मित्रार्थेऽमित्रघातिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, lord of people, there was a great battle as the Panchalas, who slew their enemies for the sake of their friends, were slaughtered by the charioteer's son."}}]}]}